From: Rafał Rojek <rafal.rojek@connectpoint.pl>
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: qcom: sc8280xp: cap Pocket S2 and FIT headphone digital volume

The Pocket S2 and KONKR Pocket FIT headphone volume is the RX digital
volume. The control spans -84..+40 dB, so exposing it as the playback
volume would map 100% of the slider to +40 dB. Limit it to 59 (-25 dB):
above that the output crackles.
---
 sound/soc/qcom/sc8280xp.c | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/sound/soc/qcom/sc8280xp.c b/sound/soc/qcom/sc8280xp.c
index d5859fb..b6bf2b9 100644
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/sc8280xp.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/sc8280xp.c
@@ -193,6 +193,19 @@ static int sc8280xp_snd_init(struct snd_soc_pcm_runtime *rtd)
 		snd_soc_limit_volume(card, "SpkrLeft PA Volume", 17);
 		snd_soc_limit_volume(card, "SpkrRight PA Volume", 17);
 		break;
+	case RX_CODEC_DMA_RX_0:
+	case RX_CODEC_DMA_RX_1:
+		/*
+		 * Pocket S2 and Pocket FIT headphones are driven from the RX
+		 * digital volume. Its range runs up to +40 dB, so cap it at
+		 * -25 dB, above which the output crackles.
+		 */
+		if (of_machine_is_compatible("ayaneo,pocket-s2") ||
+		    of_machine_is_compatible("konkr,pocket-fit")) {
+			snd_soc_limit_volume(card, "RX_RX0 Digital Volume", 59);
+			snd_soc_limit_volume(card, "RX_RX1 Digital Volume", 59);
+		}
+		break;
 	case DISPLAY_PORT_RX_0:
 		/* DISPLAY_PORT dai ids are not contiguous */
 		dp_pcm_id = 0;
